Add `src/transformation/builtins/registry.ts` exporting `builtinRegistry` with `owners`, `globalCalls` (by callee symbol name), `globalIdentifiers` (by text) and `typeFeatures` (type symbol name to the imported `LuaLibFeature`). Each owner is a plain object. `kind` is `"prototype"` or `"static"`. `diagnosticName` is the name in the `unsupported property` diagnostic. `symbolNames` lists its symbols. `prepareCall` turns the receiver, when there is one, and the arguments into `{ caller?, params }`. `methods` and `properties` hold entries by name; own properties only, nothing inherited from `Object.prototype`.

`{ kind: "lualib", feature }`: a call of that lualib feature with the receiver, when there is one, then the arguments. `{ kind: "custom", transform }`: `transform(context, node, calledMethod, call)` gets the prepared `{ caller?, params }` and returns Lua; properties use `transform(context, node)`. `{ kind: "unsupported" }`: always reported. Every member translated today has an entry; members reported by name today are `unsupported` entries (`Function`: `toString`, `name`, `arguments`, `caller`, `displayName`; `length` stays translated).

Exports `getBuiltinOwners()`, `getBuiltinOwnerForSymbol(symbolName, kind)`, `getBuiltinMethod(owner, name)`, `getBuiltinProperty(owner, name)`, `getBuiltinGlobalCall(symbolName)`, `getBuiltinGlobalIdentifier(identifierText)` and `getLuaLibTypeFeature(symbolName)`, each `undefined` when there is no entry. `getSupportedBuiltinMethods(owner)` and `getSupportedBuiltinProperties(owner)` list the member names whose entry is not `unsupported`.

Replacing or removing an entry in `builtinRegistry` before transpiling changes the emitted Lua. Every program the type checker accepts transpiles to the same Lua, with the same diagnostics, as before. Where unknown members are reported today, one with no entry is reported with the owner's `diagnosticName`. `Function` members without an entry fall through to the ordinary property and call transformation. An `Array` property access without an entry falls through; an `Array` method call without an entry is reported. Unchanged: the `Object.prototype` fallback for `toString` and `hasOwnProperty`, the optional-call diagnostic for static builtins, the lualib feature imports, receiver and argument order.
